Description: libcamera: camera_lens: keep the lens subdev open only while streaming
 CameraLens opened the lens subdev in init() and kept it open for the life
 of the CameraManager. Lens drivers power the actuator while their node is
 open: dw9719 (the GT9764 VCM of the TB323FU rear camera) takes a runtime
 PM reference in its open handler. In a desktop session PipeWire and
 WirePlumber each keep a CameraManager for the whole session, so the VCM
 regulator (vreg_l6b_2p8) stayed on and the lens stayed driven with no
 camera in use.
 .
 CameraLens:
  - init() closes the subdev once the driver is validated and the model
    and controls are cached. That instance is never reopened, so controls()
    and its ControlId pointers stay valid and unchanged.
  - open() opens a separate, new V4L2Subdevice instance (a no-op when
    open), close() destroys it, isOpen() reports it.
  - setFocusPosition() opens the lens on demand. The IPU3 and Raspberry Pi
    pipeline handlers, which never call open() or close(), keep working:
    the lens opens on their first focus write and stays open as before,
    just no longer from CameraManager start. They are deliberately not
    made to close at stop: the Raspberry Pi IPA sends its default lens
    position only on the first start, so the lens would be left at rest
    while the IPA assumes otherwise.
 .
 Simple pipeline handler:
  - start() opens the lens just before streamon. Failure is a warning,
    not a start failure; autofocus then reports AfStateFailed.
  - stopDevice() closes it last, after the software ISP has stopped and
    delivered its pending metadata. dw9719 then ramps the lens down to 0
    and cuts its supplies in its runtime suspend handler, after its 1 s
    autosuspend delay, so no userspace parking is needed.
  - moveFocus() refuses to move a closed lens instead of letting
    CameraLens reopen it outside the start()..stop() window.
  - A lens failure no longer fails the request: handleFocusControls()
    returns void, the frame is captured and AfState reports the failure.
  - resetAutoFocus() also clears afCurrentFrame_ and afMoveFrame_. Request
    sequence numbers restart at 0 on every start, and the stale values of
    the previous run held the first scan back for as many frames as that
    run lasted (a bug of patch 0004).
  - updateAutoFocus() returns early for a camera without a focus lens, as
    handleFocusControls() already did. As in iceland-mainline, patches
    0003-0004 attached AfMode, AfState and FocusAbsolute to every completed
    request of a fixed-focus camera (the TB323FU front camera), which
    advertises none of these controls, telling applications it could focus.
 .
 Everything runs in the pipeline handler thread, as before.
