  * The CameraLens class eases handling of lens for pipeline handlers by
  * hiding the details of the V4L2 subdevice kernel API and caching lens
  * information.
+ *
+ * Lens actuator drivers commonly power the actuator for as long as their
+ * subdev node is open: the dw9719 driver, for instance, takes a runtime PM
+ * reference in its subdev open handler and drops it in the close handler. A
+ * CameraLens lives as long as the CameraManager that created it, which for a
+ * desktop media server means the whole session, so the subdev node is only
+ * kept open while it is needed. init() closes it again once the lens
+ * information has been cached, and the node is reopened by open(), or on
+ * demand by setFocusPosition(), and closed by close().
+ *
+ * The lens information returned by controls() is cached at init() time and
+ * stays valid, unchanged, whether the lens is open or not.
+ *
+ * CameraLens is not thread-safe. All functions shall be called from the
+ * thread that runs the pipeline handler.
  */
 
